IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `spi61-rules`

§ `Tests`

GIVEN adj IS A NUMBER, act IS A NUMBER, ctb IS A NUMBER, k IS A `Prescribed amount case`, prior IS A NUMBER, wid IS A BOOLEAN, exc IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Pension increase case`
`case` adj `/` act `/` ctb `,` k `,` prior `,` wid `,` exc MEANS
    `Pension increase case` OF adj, act, ctb, k, 0, prior, wid, exc, Date 1 1 1962

-- 3 additional units at £32 10s: £97 10s.
#ASSERT `my annual pension increase for` (`case` 10 `/` 7 `/` 7 `,` `the standard case` `,` 0 `,` FALSE `,` FALSE) EQUALS 97.5
#ASSERT `my annual pension increase for` (`case` 7 `/` 7 `/` 7 `,` `the standard case` `,` 0 `,` FALSE `,` FALSE) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `my annual pension increase for` (`case` 6 `/` 7 `/` 7 `,` `the standard case` `,` 0 `,` FALSE `,` FALSE) EQUALS 0
-- (b): 6 of 8 units contributed: £24 7s 6d a unit; 2 additional units: £48 15s.
#ASSERT `my annual pension increase for` (`case` 10 `/` 8 `/` 6 `,` `contributed for fewer units than entitled` `,` 0 `,` FALSE `,` FALSE) EQUALS 48.75
-- s 4(2): less a £40 increase under the 1957 Act.
#ASSERT `my annual pension increase for` (`case` 10 `/` 7 `/` 7 `,` `the standard case` `,` 40 `,` FALSE `,` FALSE) EQUALS 57.5
#ASSERT `my annual pension increase for` (`case` 10 `/` 7 `/` 7 `,` `the standard case` `,` 100 `,` FALSE `,` FALSE) EQUALS 0
-- s 4(4): five-eighths for a widow.
#ASSERT `my annual pension increase for` (`case` 10 `/` 7 `/` 7 `,` `the standard case` `,` 0 `,` TRUE `,` FALSE) EQUALS 60.9375
#ASSERT `my annual pension increase for` (`case` 10 `/` 7 `/` 7 `,` `the standard case` `,` 0 `,` FALSE `,` TRUE) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `my annual pension increase for` (`Pension increase case` OF 10, 7, 7, `a case under paragraph (c) or (d)`, 1/2, 0, FALSE, FALSE, Date 1 1 1962) EQUALS 48.75
